# Sentiment Analysis Using Machine Learning

## Overview

This project implements a simple Sentiment Analysis model using Python and Scikit-Learn.

The goal is to classify movie reviews as Positive or Negative using a Naive Bayes classifier.

## Dataset

A small dataset of positive and negative movie reviews was created for training and testing.

## Technologies Used

* Python
* Scikit-Learn
* Naive Bayes
* CountVectorizer

## Workflow

1. Create sentiment dataset
2. Convert text into numerical features
3. Split dataset into training and testing sets
4. Train Naive Bayes classifier
5. Evaluate using accuracy score
6. Test on new custom reviews

## Accuracy

The model achieved a good accuracy score on the test dataset.

## Manual Test Cases

### Positive

* I really loved this film
* Amazing performance
* Fantastic experience

### Negative

* This movie was horrible
* Not good at all

## Observations

1. More training data improves model accuracy.
2. Unknown words can reduce prediction quality.
3. Balanced datasets produce better results.

## Limitations

* Does not understand sarcasm.
* Struggles with mixed sentiments.
* Small datasets limit performance.

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates the basic workflow of text classification and sentiment analysis using Machine Learning.

